 "source_note": "Physical facts from NTSB Highway Accident Report NTSB/HAR-17/02 (accident ID HWY16FH018). Witnesses A, B and C are FICTIONAL. No real names or brand names are used. Fictional testimony describes only vehicle movements and visibility, never any real person's conduct or state. Values marked 'assumed' or 'derived' are modeling choices, not NTSB findings.",
 "summary": "At 4:36 p.m. on a clear, dry afternoon, a passenger car (Vehicle A) traveling east on four-lane divided US-27A at about 74 mph struck the right side of a tractor-semitrailer (Vehicle T) that was turning left from the westbound left-turn lane, across the eastbound lanes, onto NE 140th Court. The car passed under the trailer, left the road to the right, went through a culvert and two fences, broke a utility pole and came to rest about 910 ft beyond the impact. No pre-impact tire marks were found. A vertical crest 1,132 ft west of the intersection was the only sight restriction, and NTSB computed up to 10.4 s of mutual sight time.",
 "timeOfDay": "16:36",
 "lighting": "day",
 "weather": "clear, dry pavement; sun high and behind the eastbound car",
 "coordinate_frame_note": "Meters. Y up, ground y=0 at the intersection. +X = east (direction of travel of Vehicle A), -Z = north. Origin = initial point of impact: center of the right (outside) eastbound lane at the centerline of NE 140th Court. Eastbound lanes are south of the median (z>-5.5), westbound north of it. NE 140th Court is modeled as running due south (+Z) from x=0; the real 109-degree skew is ignored. Eastbound approach descends at 2.15% from the crest at x=-345 m (road at the crest is y\u2248+7.4 m) to x\u2248+99.7 m, then is effectively flat; a WORLD may model the slope or keep flat ground (the crest is ~345 m away and does not affect the witness sightlines). Heading_deg is a compass bearing: 0=north(-Z), 90=east(+X), 180=south(+Z), 270/-90=west(-X). Event clock t=0 is when the car is at the crest (10.43 s before impact).",
